# Element Armory – Task Roadmap

---

## Email Templates — Immediate
- [x] Welcome email (`server/src/emails/welcome.tsx`) — fires on account creation via databaseHooks
- [x] Magic link email polish (`server/src/emails/magic-link.tsx`) — Hr separator, shared styles
- [x] Shared email styles (`server/src/emails/styles.ts`) — Element Armory tokens

---

## Email Templates — Onboarding Series
- [ ] 24h reminder — "You signed up yesterday, have you tried capturing your first element?"
- [ ] Day 3–5 value email — show a compelling use-case; link to docs or example captures

---

## Email Templates — Event-Based
- [ ] First capture — "You captured your first element. Here's what to do with it."
- [ ] 3rd–5th capture — soft nudge toward creating an account (anonymous → account conversion)
- [ ] 10th capture milestone — celebrate; introduce AI rebuild / Pro features
- [ ] Limit reached — explain quota; offer path to free account or Pro upgrade
- [ ] Post-limit follow-up (48h) — re-engage users who hit their limit but haven't upgraded

---

## Email Templates — Anonymous → Account Conversion
- [ ] "Save your work" email — triggered when anonymous install approaches limit; explain account benefits (sync, library, higher quota)

---

## Email Templates — Retention / Lifecycle
- [ ] Weekly capture summary — "You captured N elements this week"
- [ ] Inactive reactivation — 14d or 30d no captures; "still there?"
- [ ] Feature updates / changelog — announce new capture types, AI rebuild improvements, etc.

---

## Email Infrastructure
- [x] Email send logging + open & click tracking — `email_sends` + `email_clicks` tables; tracking pixel + redirect endpoints at `/api/email/track/`
- [ ] Unsubscribe / suppression list — honour opt-outs; store suppressed emails in DB; check before every send
- [ ] Email send deduplication / idempotency — prevent duplicate sends on retry or hook re-fire
- [ ] Preview server — `react-email dev` script in `server/package.json`; document usage in README

---

## Chrome Extension — Entitlement Tiers

### Anonymous (no account)
- 10 captures / month
- Local storage only — no cloud sync
- No library view
- No AI rebuild

### Free account
- 20 captures / month
- Cloud sync
- Library view
- No AI rebuild

### Pro account
- Unlimited captures
- Cloud sync
- Library view
- AI rebuild (MCP)
- Export formats (HTML, JSX, CSS, JSON)

---

## Extension In-Product Prompts
- [ ] Capture count meter in popup — show `used / limit` with visual progress
- [ ] Paywall prompt at limit — clear message, direct link to upgrade
- [ ] "Create account" nudge for anonymous users after 5 captures — explain sync and higher quota

---

## Capture Counting + Quota Enforcement
- [ ] Server-side capture count per install and per user per billing period
- [ ] Return `quota_used` and `quota_limit` in entitlements endpoint (`GET /api/billing/entitlement`)
- [ ] Enforce at capture creation:
  - Anonymous over limit → 402 with `quota_reached` error code
  - Free account over limit → 402 with upgrade URL
  - Pro → pass through

---

## Event Tracking
- [ ] `user.created` event — stored in DB or emitted to event bus; used to trigger welcome email
- [ ] `capture.created` event — include running count; used for milestone emails
- [ ] `quota.reached` event — fire once per billing period; triggers limit email

---

## Background Job Queue
- [ ] Email scheduling infrastructure — queue and deliver time-based emails (24h reminder, day 3–5)
- [ ] Job runner options: simple DB-backed queue (SQLite), or BullMQ / pg-boss if moving to Postgres
- [ ] Dead-letter handling and retry policy

---

## MCP Server — Phase 6
- [ ] Run on separate port from Express API
- [ ] MCP tools call existing `src/services/` — no duplicate business logic
- [ ] Auth: accept app-issued tokens; validate per-request; map to user / install
- [ ] Chrome extension: "Copy MCP config" flow — generate connection config for Cursor, Claude Desktop, etc.
- [ ] Tokens: scoped, revocable

---

## Hosted App Polish — Phase 7
- [ ] Library / history view for captures (paginated, filterable)
- [ ] Sign-out: remove account link from install; captures remain
- [ ] Nightly DB backup to S3 with retention policy
- [ ] Monitoring, request logging, error tracking
